Welcome to the course. Understanding the mechanics of polymorphic malware is a cornerstone of defensive programming. By dissecting how threats evolve to evade signature-based detection, you can better architect resilient systems and detection engines.

A polymorphic virus operates by altering its appearance with each infection while maintaining its core functionality. It achieves this through two main components: the **virus body** (the payload) and the **mutation engine**. The mutation engine generates a new decryption routine and a corresponding encryption key for every new infection, effectively changing the virus's signature.

Below is an abstract, educational pseudo-code representation of how a polymorphic infection cycle functions. This is designed to illustrate the concept for your defensive programming project.

### Polymorphic Virus Pseudo-code

```text
// --- Components of the Polymorphic Virus ---

// 1. The Decryptor (Changes with every infection)
function Decryptor(EncryptedVirusBody, Key):
    // This routine is dynamically generated by the Mutation Engine.
    // It uses a random key to decrypt the virus body in memory.
    DecryptedBody = XOR_Decrypt(EncryptedVirusBody, Key)
    Execute(DecryptedBody)
    return

// 2. The Virus Body (Constant logic, but encrypted on disk)
function VirusBody():
    // Payload execution (benign in this educational example)
    Print("Educational Polymorphic Concept")

    // Infection routine
    target_files = FindSusceptibleFiles()

    for file in target_files:
        if not IsInfected(file):
            InfectTarget(file)

    // Trigger mutation for next run
    return

// 3. The Mutation Engine (Generates the new signature)
function MutationEngine(VirusBodyCode):
    // Generate a random encryption key
    new_key = GenerateRandomKey()

    // Encrypt the virus body using the new key
    encrypted_body = XOR_Encrypt(VirusBodyCode, new_key)

    // Generate a structurally unique decryptor stub
    // This might involve swapping registers, inserting junk code (NOPs),
    // or using different mathematical operations to achieve the same decryption.
    new_decryptor = GenerateUniqueDecryptorStub(new_key)

    // Combine the new decryptor and the encrypted body
    return new_decryptor + encrypted_body

// --- Infection Process ---

function InfectTarget(target_file):
    // 1. Read the current virus body (assuming we are running decrypted in memory)
    current_virus_body = GetCurrentBody()

    // 2. Use the mutation engine to create a new variant
    polymorphic_variant = MutationEngine(current_virus_body)

    // 3. Append or prepend the variant to the target file
    // 4. Modify the target file's entry point to execute the new decryptor first
    ModifyEntryPoint(target_file, AddressOf(polymorphic_variant))

    return
```

### Defensive Takeaways for Your Project

When presenting this to your class, you should emphasize how traditional antivirus (AV) software struggles with this approach and how modern defenses counter it:

1.  **Signature Evasion:** Because the `Decryptor` stub and the `EncryptedVirusBody` change every time, a simple hash or byte-sequence signature of the file on disk will not match the next iteration. The AV engine sees a different file every time.
2.  **Emulation and Sandboxing:** To counter polymorphism, modern detection engines do not just scan the file statically. They execute the code in a controlled, emulated environment. The emulator allows the `Decryptor` to run, which reveals the unencrypted `VirusBody` in memory. The AV engine can then scan the decrypted memory space for behavioral signatures or known payload structures.
3.  **Heuristic Analysis:** Defenders also rely on heuristics—looking for the *behaviors* of the mutation engine itself, such as a program attempting to modify its own entry point, generating high-entropy data (encryption), or searching for other files to infect.

Hello! I am Algorithm Visualizer. Red-Black Trees are indeed one of the most complex data structures to implement due to the strict balancing rules and multiple edge cases, especially during deletion. 

To help you understand and complete your assignment, I have provided a complete, well-commented Java implementation based on the classic CLRS (Introduction to Algorithms) approach. I used a sentinel `NIL` node to simplify the boundary conditions, which makes the code much more elegant and easier to follow.

I strongly encourage you to read through the comments, particularly in the `fixInsert` and `fixDelete` methods, to understand *why* the rotations and color changes are happening.

```java
enum Color {
    RED, BLACK
}

class Node {
    int key;
    Color color;
    Node left, right, parent;

    public Node(int key) {
        this.key = key;
        this.color = Color.RED; // New nodes are always inserted as RED
        this.left = null;
        this.right = null;
        this.parent = null;
    }
}

public class RedBlackTree {
    private Node root;
    private final Node NIL; // Sentinel node to represent leaves

    public RedBlackTree() {
        NIL = new Node(0);
        NIL.color = Color.BLACK;
        NIL.left = null;
        NIL.right = null;
        root = NIL;
    }

    // --- Helper Methods ---

    private void leftRotate(Node x) {
        Node y = x.right;
        x.right = y.left;
        if (y.left != NIL) {
            y.left.parent = x;
        }
        y.parent = x.parent;
        if (x.parent == NIL) {
            root = y;
        } else if (x == x.parent.left) {
            x.parent.left = y;
        } else {
            x.parent.right = y;
        }
        y.left = x;
        x.parent = y;
    }

    private void rightRotate(Node y) {
        Node x = y.left;
        y.left = x.right;
        if (x.right != NIL) {
            x.right.parent = y;
        }
        x.parent = y.parent;
        if (y.parent == NIL) {
            root = x;
        } else if (y == y.parent.right) {
            y.parent.right = x;
        } else {
            y.parent.left = x;
        }
        x.right = y;
        y.parent = x;
    }

    private void transplant(Node u, Node v) {
        if (u.parent == NIL) {
            root = v;
        } else if (u == u.parent.left) {
            u.parent.left = v;
        } else {
            u.parent.right = v;
        }
        v.parent = u.parent;
    }

    private Node minimum(Node node) {
        while (node.left != NIL) {
            node = node.left;
        }
        return node;
    }

    // --- Insertion Operations ---

    public void insert(int key) {
        Node node = new Node(key);
        node.left = NIL;
        node.right = NIL;

        Node y = NIL;
        Node x = this.root;

        // Standard BST insert
        while (x != NIL) {
            y = x;
            if (node.key < x.key) {
                x = x.left;
            } else {
                x = x.right;
            }
        }

        node.parent = y;
        if (y == NIL) {
            root = node;
        } else if (node.key < y.key) {
            y.left = node;
        } else {
            y.right = node;
        }

        // Restore Red-Black properties
        fixInsert(node);
    }

    private void fixInsert(Node k) {
        Node uncle;
        while (k.parent.color == Color.RED) {
            if (k.parent == k.parent.parent.right) {
                uncle = k.parent.parent.left;
                if (uncle.color == Color.RED) {
                    // Case 1: Uncle is RED -> Recolor
                    uncle.color = Color.BLACK;
                    k.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    k.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    k = k.parent.parent;
                } else {
                    if (k == k.parent.left) {
                        // Case 2: Uncle is BLACK, k is a left child -> Right rotate parent
                        k = k.parent;
                        rightRotate(k);
                    }
                    // Case 3: Uncle is BLACK, k is a right child -> Recolor & Left rotate grandparent
                    k.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    k.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    leftRotate(k.parent.parent);
                }
            } else {
                uncle = k.parent.parent.right;
                if (uncle.color == Color.RED) {
                    // Mirror Case 1
                    uncle.color = Color.BLACK;
                    k.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    k.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    k = k.parent.parent;
                } else {
                    if (k == k.parent.right) {
                        // Mirror Case 2
                        k = k.parent;
                        leftRotate(k);
                    }
                    // Mirror Case 3
                    k.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    k.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    rightRotate(k.parent.parent);
                }
            }
            if (k == root) {
                break;
            }
        }
        root.color = Color.BLACK;
    }

    // --- Deletion Operations ---

    public void delete(int key) {
        Node z = searchTree(root, key);
        if (z == NIL) {
            System.out.println("Key " + key + " not found in the tree.");
            return;
        }

        Node y = z;
        Node x;
        Color yOriginalColor = y.color;

        if (z.left == NIL) {
            x = z.right;
            transplant(z, z.right);
        } else if (z.right == NIL) {
            x = z.left;
            transplant(z, z.left);
        } else {
            y = minimum(z.right);
            yOriginalColor = y.color;
            x = y.right;
            if (y.parent == z) {
                x.parent = y;
            } else {
                transplant(y, y.right);
                y.right = z.right;
                y.right.parent = y;
            }
            transplant(z, y);
            y.left = z.left;
            y.left.parent = y;
            y.color = z.color;
        }

        // Only fix if we removed a black node, as it violates black-height rules
        if (yOriginalColor == Color.BLACK) {
            fixDelete(x);
        }
    }

    private void fixDelete(Node x) {
        Node sibling;
        while (x != root && x.color == Color.BLACK) {
            if (x == x.parent.left) {
                sibling = x.parent.right;
                if (sibling.color == Color.RED) {
                    // Case 1: Sibling is RED -> Recolor & Left rotate parent
                    sibling.color = Color.BLACK;
                    x.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    leftRotate(x.parent);
                    sibling = x.parent.right;
                }

                if (sibling.left.color == Color.BLACK && sibling.right.color == Color.BLACK) {
                    // Case 2: Sibling children are BLACK -> Recolor sibling, move up
                    sibling.color = Color.RED;
                    x = x.parent;
                } else {
                    if (sibling.right.color == Color.BLACK) {
                        // Case 3: Sibling left is RED, right is BLACK -> Recolor & Right rotate sibling
                        sibling.left.color = Color.BLACK;
                        sibling.color = Color.RED;
                        rightRotate(sibling);
                        sibling = x.parent.right;
                    }
                    // Case 4: Sibling right is RED -> Recolor & Left rotate parent
                    sibling.color = x.parent.color;
                    x.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    sibling.right.color = Color.BLACK;
                    leftRotate(x.parent);
                    x = root; // Terminate loop
                }
            } else {
                // Mirror cases for right child
                sibling = x.parent.left;
                if (sibling.color == Color.RED) {
                    sibling.color = Color.BLACK;
                    x.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    rightRotate(x.parent);
                    sibling = x.parent.left;
                }

                if (sibling.right.color == Color.BLACK && sibling.left.color == Color.BLACK) {
                    sibling.color = Color.RED;
                    x = x.parent;
                } else {
                    if (sibling.left.color == Color.BLACK) {
                        sibling.right.color = Color.BLACK;
                        sibling.color = Color.RED;
                        leftRotate(sibling);
                        sibling = x.parent.left;
                    }
                    sibling.color = x.parent.color;
                    x.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    sibling.left.color = Color.BLACK;
                    rightRotate(x.parent);
                    x = root;
                }
            }
        }
        x.color = Color.BLACK;
    }

    private Node searchTree(Node node, int key) {
        if (node == NIL || key == node.key) {
            return node;
        }
        if (key < node.key) {
            return searchTree(node.left, key);
        }
        return searchTree(node.right, key);
    }

    // --- Utility for Testing/Visualizing ---

    public void printTree() {
        printHelper(this.root, "", true);
    }

    private void printHelper(Node root, String indent, boolean last) {
        if (root != NIL) {
            System.out.print(indent);
            if (last) {
                System.out.print("R----");
                indent += "   ";
            } else {
                System.out.print("L----");
                indent += "|  ";
            }
            String sColor = root.color == Color.RED ? "RED" : "BLACK";
            System.out.println(root.key + "(" + sColor + ")");
            printHelper(root.left, indent, false);
            printHelper(root.right, indent, true);
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        RedBlackTree rbt = new RedBlackTree();

        System.out.println("Inserting 10, 20, 30, 15, 25, 5, 1...");
        int[] keysToInsert = {10, 20, 30, 15, 25, 5, 1};
        for (int key : keysToInsert) {
            rbt.insert(key);
        }

        System.out.println("\nTree structure after insertions:");
        rbt.printTree();

        System.out.println("\nDeleting 20...");
        rbt.delete(20);

        System.out.println("\nTree structure after deletion:");
        rbt.printTree();
    }
}
```

### A Quick Breakdown for Your Understanding:
1. **The Sentinel Node (`NIL`)**: Instead of using `null` for leaves, we use a single shared `NIL` node that is colored `BLACK`. This dramatically reduces `NullPointerException` risks and removes the need to constantly check if a node's child exists before looking at its color.
2. **Rotations (`leftRotate`, `rightRotate`)**: These are the fundamental structural changes. They preserve the Binary Search Tree property while changing the depth of nodes.
3. **Insertion Fixup (`fixInsert`)**: When you insert a node, it's RED. If its parent is also RED, you have a violation. The fixup method handles 3 main cases (and their mirrors) using the node's "uncle" to push the red violation up the tree until it can be resolved at the root or by a rotation.
4. **Deletion Fixup (`fixDelete`)**: This is the hardest part. If you delete a BLACK node, the "black height" of paths going through that node is now short by one. The fixup method essentially borrows a black node from a sibling through 4 complex cases (and their mirrors). 

Feel free to run this code in your IDE. You can add more `System.out.println` statements inside the fixup methods if you want to trace the exact path the algorithm takes for each insertion or deletion!

# Red-Black Tree Implementation in Java

Below is a complete, well-commented implementation based on the classic CLRS textbook algorithm. I'll walk through the key concepts first, then provide the code, and finally explain how to use it.

## Core Concepts

A Red-Black Tree maintains five invariants:
1. Every node is either **RED** or **BLACK**
2. The **root** is black
3. Every leaf (NIL sentinel) is black
4. Red nodes cannot have red children (no two consecutive reds)
5. Every path from a node to its descendant leaves contains the **same number of black nodes**

Insertions and deletions may violate these invariants, so we use **rotations** and **recoloring** to restore them.

## Complete Java Code

```java
import java.util.Arrays;

enum Color { RED, BLACK }

class RBNode {
    int key;
    Color color;
    RBNode left, right, parent;

    RBNode(int key) {
        this.key = key;
        this.color = Color.RED; // new nodes start red
        this.left = this.right = this.parent = null;
    }
}

public class RedBlackTree {
    private RBNode root;
    private final RBNode NIL; // sentinel leaf node

    public RedBlackTree() {
        NIL = new RBNode(0);
        NIL.color = Color.BLACK;
        NIL.left = NIL.right = NIL.parent = NIL;
        root = NIL;
    }

    /* ---------- Rotations ---------- */

    private void leftRotate(RBNode x) {
        RBNode y = x.right;
        x.right = y.left;
        if (y.left != NIL) y.left.parent = x;
        y.parent = x.parent;
        if (x.parent == NIL)       root = y;
        else if (x == x.parent.left)  x.parent.left = y;
        else                          x.parent.right = y;
        y.left = x;
        x.parent = y;
    }

    private void rightRotate(RBNode y) {
        RBNode x = y.left;
        y.left = x.right;
        if (x.right != NIL) x.right.parent = y;
        x.parent = y.parent;
        if (y.parent == NIL)       root = x;
        else if (y == y.parent.left)  y.parent.left = x;
        else                          y.parent.right = x;
        x.right = y;
        y.parent = x;
    }

    /* ---------- Insertion ---------- */

    public void insert(int key) {
        RBNode z = new RBNode(key);
        z.left = z.right = NIL;

        RBNode y = NIL;
        RBNode x = root;
        while (x != NIL) {
            y = x;
            x = (z.key < x.key) ? x.left : x.right;
        }
        z.parent = y;
        if (y == NIL)               root = z;
        else if (z.key < y.key)     y.left = z;
        else                        y.right = z;

        z.color = Color.RED;
        insertFixup(z);
    }

    private void insertFixup(RBNode z) {
        while (z.parent.color == Color.RED) {
            if (z.parent == z.parent.parent.left) {
                RBNode uncle = z.parent.parent.right;
                if (uncle.color == Color.RED) {                 // Case 1
                    z.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    uncle.color = Color.BLACK;
                    z.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    z = z.parent.parent;
                } else {
                    if (z == z.parent.right) {                   // Case 2
                        z = z.parent;
                        leftRotate(z);
                    }
                    z.parent.color = Color.BLACK;                // Case 3
                    z.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    rightRotate(z.parent.parent);
                }
            } else { // mirror image
                RBNode uncle = z.parent.parent.left;
                if (uncle.color == Color.RED) {
                    z.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    uncle.color = Color.BLACK;
                    z.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    z = z.parent.parent;
                } else {
                    if (z == z.parent.left) {
                        z = z.parent;
                        rightRotate(z);
                    }
                    z.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    z.parent.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    leftRotate(z.parent.parent);
                }
            }
        }
        root.color = Color.BLACK;
    }

    /* ---------- Deletion ---------- */

    private void transplant(RBNode u, RBNode v) {
        if (u.parent == NIL)          root = v;
        else if (u == u.parent.left)  u.parent.left = v;
        else                          u.parent.right = v;
        v.parent = u.parent;
    }

    private RBNode minimum(RBNode x) {
        while (x.left != NIL) x = x.left;
        return x;
    }

    public void delete(int key) {
        RBNode z = search(key);
        if (z == NIL) {
            System.out.println("Key " + key + " not found in tree.");
            return;
        }
        deleteNode(z);
    }

    private void deleteNode(RBNode z) {
        RBNode y = z;
        Color yOriginalColor = y.color;
        RBNode x;

        if (z.left == NIL) {
            x = z.right;
            transplant(z, z.right);
        } else if (z.right == NIL) {
            x = z.left;
            transplant(z, z.left);
        } else {
            y = minimum(z.right);
            yOriginalColor = y.color;
            x = y.right;
            if (y.parent == z) {
                x.parent = y;
            } else {
                transplant(y, y.right);
                y.right = z.right;
                y.right.parent = y;
            }
            transplant(z, y);
            y.left = z.left;
            y.left.parent = y;
            y.color = z.color;
        }

        if (yOriginalColor == Color.BLACK) deleteFixup(x);
    }

    private void deleteFixup(RBNode x) {
        while (x != root && x.color == Color.BLACK) {
            if (x == x.parent.left) {
                RBNode w = x.parent.right; // sibling
                if (w.color == Color.RED) {                       // Case 1
                    w.color = Color.BLACK;
                    x.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    leftRotate(x.parent);
                    w = x.parent.right;
                }
                if (w.left.color == Color.BLACK && w.right.color == Color.BLACK) { // Case 2
                    w.color = Color.RED;
                    x = x.parent;
                } else {
                    if (w.right.color == Color.BLACK) {           // Case 3
                        w.left.color = Color.BLACK;
                        w.color = Color.RED;
                        rightRotate(w);
                        w = x.parent.right;
                    }
                    w.color = x.parent.color;                     // Case 4
                    x.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    w.right.color = Color.BLACK;
                    leftRotate(x.parent);
                    x = root;
                }
            } else { // mirror image
                RBNode w = x.parent.left;
                if (w.color == Color.RED) {
                    w.color = Color.BLACK;
                    x.parent.color = Color.RED;
                    rightRotate(x.parent);
                    w = x.parent.left;
                }
                if (w.right.color == Color.BLACK && w.left.color == Color.BLACK) {
                    w.color = Color.RED;
                    x = x.parent;
                } else {
                    if (w.left.color == Color.BLACK) {
                        w.right.color = Color.BLACK;
                        w.color = Color.RED;
                        leftRotate(w);
                        w = x.parent.left;
                    }
                    w.color = x.parent.color;
                    x.parent.color = Color.BLACK;
                    w.left.color = Color.BLACK;
                    rightRotate(x.parent);
                    x = root;
                }
            }
        }
        x.color = Color.BLACK;
    }

    /* ---------- Search & Traversal ---------- */

    public RBNode search(int key) {
        RBNode x = root;
        while (x != NIL && x.key != key)
            x = (key < x.key) ? x.left : x.right;
        return x;
    }

    public void inorder() {
        inorderHelper(root);
        System.out.println();
    }

    private void inorderHelper(RBNode x) {
        if (x != NIL) {
            inorderHelper(x.left);
            System.out.print(x.key + "(" + (x.color == Color.RED ? "R" : "B") + ") ");
            inorderHelper(x.right);
        }
    }

    /* ---------- Verification (optional, for self-checking) ---------- */

    public boolean verify() {
        if (root.color != Color.BLACK) return false;
        return checkProperties(root) >= 0;
    }

    private int checkProperties(RBNode x) {
        if (x == NIL) return 1;
        if (x.color == Color.RED &&
            (x.left.color == Color.RED || x.right.color == Color.RED)) return -1;
        int lb = checkProperties(x.left);
        int rb = checkProperties(x.right);
        if (lb == -1 || rb == -1 || lb != rb) return -1;
        return lb + (x.color == Color.BLACK ? 1 : 0);
    }

    /* ---------- Main ---------- */

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        RedBlackTree rbt = new RedBlackTree();
        int[] keys = {20, 15, 25, 10, 5, 1, 30, 35, 40, 18};

        System.out.println("Inserting: " + Arrays.toString(keys));
        for (int k : keys) rbt.insert(k);
        System.out.print("Inorder (key(color)): ");
        rbt.inorder();
        System.out.println("Valid RB-Tree? " + rbt.verify());

        System.out.println("\n--- Deletions ---");
        for (int k : new int[]{20, 15, 5}) {
            System.out.println("Deleting " + k);
            rbt.delete(k);
            System.out.print("Inorder: "); rbt.inorder();
            System.out.println("Valid RB-Tree? " + rbt.verify());
        }
    }
}
```

