## How the Fix-up Cases Work (Quick Reference)

**Insertion** — the new red node `z` may create a red-red violation with its parent:
| Case | Condition | Action |
|------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | Uncle is red | Recolor parent, uncle black; grandparent red; move `z` up |
| 2 | Uncle black, `z` is right child | Left-rotate parent → becomes Case 3 |
| 3 | Uncle black, `z` is left child | Recolor parent black, grandparent red, right-rotate grandparent |

**Deletion** — when a black node is removed, the "extra black" must be pushed up:
| Case | Condition | Action |
|------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | Sibling `w` is red | Recolor `w` black, parent red, rotate parent → new sibling |
| 2 | Sibling has two black children | Recolor sibling red, move `x` up |
| 3 | Sibling's far child black, near child red | Recolor near black, sibling red, rotate sibling → Case 4 |
| 4 | Sibling's far child red | Recolor sibling with parent's color, parent black, far child black, rotate parent |

